---
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import InstallCommand from "../../components/InstallCommand.astro";
import PluginReference from "../../components/PluginReference.astro";
import { getPlugin } from "../../data/plugins";
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";

const plugin = getPlugin("autobuild")!;

const tocEntries = [
  { id: "what-it-does", text: "What it does", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "install", text: "Install", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "register", text: "Register", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "how-it-fires", text: "How it fires", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "no-component", text: "No component", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "props", text: "Props", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "for-agents", text: "For agents", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
];
---

<Doc
  tocEntries={tocEntries}
  currentSlug="autobuild"
  title="autobuild"
  section="@plugdash/autobuild"
  description="Rebuild a static EmDash site when you publish."
>
  <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
  <p>
    For static and prerendered sites that read EmDash content at build
    time. autobuild calls a Cloudflare Pages, Netlify or Vercel deploy
    hook when a post is published or unpublished, or when a published post
    is deleted. Autosaves do not trigger it. It waits
    <code>debounceMs</code> (default 5 seconds), so a burst of publishes
    makes one request. A failed request is logged and never fails the
    publish. No companion component.
  </p>
  <p>
    A server-rendered EmDash site (<code>output: "server"</code>, the
    default in every template) shows new content at once and does not
    need it. plugdash.dev is server-rendered, so it does not use
    autobuild.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <InstallCommand command={plugin.installCommand} />

  <h2 id="register">Register</h2>
  <Code language="js" filename="astro.config.mjs" code={`import { defineConfig } from "astro/config"
import emdash from "emdash/astro"
import { autobuildPlugin } from "@plugdash/autobuild"

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [
    emdash({
      plugins: [
        autobuildPlugin({
          hookUrl: process.env.DEPLOY_HOOK_URL,
          collections: ["posts"],
        }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
})`} />
  <p>
    Keep the hook URL in an environment variable and never commit it. Or
    leave <code>hookUrl</code> out and paste the URL in the admin under
    Plugins, Autobuild, field <strong>Deploy hook URL</strong>. That is a
    secret setting, so the server needs <code>EMDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>
    (<code>pnpm exec emdash secrets generate</code>; a Worker secret on
    Cloudflare). The admin value wins over the option.
  </p>
  <p>
    The URL must be https and its host must be
    <code>api.cloudflare.com</code>, <code>api.netlify.com</code>,
    <code>api.vercel.com</code>, the host of the <code>hookUrl</code>
    option, or a host you add to <code>allowedHosts</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-it-fires">How it fires</h2>
  <pre><code>publish in admin -&gt; wait debounceMs -&gt; hook fires -&gt; your host builds -&gt; live</code></pre>
  <p>
    Hooks: <code>content:afterPublish</code>,
    <code>content:afterUnpublish</code> and <code>content:afterDelete</code>
    (only for entries that were published). It does not retry a failed
    deploy; the next publish does.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-component">No component</h2>
  <p>
    autobuild has no companion component. It is infrastructure only.
  </p>

  <PluginReference plugin={plugin} />

  <h2 id="for-agents">For agents</h2>
  <p>
    Only install autobuild on a static or prerendered site. On a
    server-rendered site, skip it. After registering
    <code>autobuildPlugin(&#123; hookUrl: process.env.DEPLOY_HOOK_URL &#125;)</code>,
    publish a post and confirm a build starts on the host within a few
    seconds. With no hook URL the plugin logs
    <code>no hook URL configured, deploys are off</code> once and does
    nothing. Data stored: a debounce token in plugin KV.
  </p>
</Doc>
